{"id":"e01t1","name":"Daily Revenue from Raw Ride Files","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A ride-hailing company drops one CSV file per city and per day into a folder. Files come from different city teams, so header names and number formats are not consistent. Finance needs one table with the completed revenue per city and per day.</p>\n<p>Implement <code>solve(spark, input_dir)</code>. Every file in <code>input_dir</code> has a header line and the columns below, always in this order:</p>\n<ul><li><code>ride_id</code> - the ID of the ride. Because of a retry bug, the same ride can appear in two files;</li><li><code>status</code> - the status of the ride, for example <code>\"COMPLETED\"</code>, <code>\" completed \"</code> or <code>\"cancelled\"</code>;</li><li><code>fare_mad</code> - the fare in dirhams, written <code>\"45.50\"</code>, <code>\"30,00\"</code>, empty, or with a typo such as <code>\"4O.00\"</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>Header names may contain extra spaces and capital letters. File names follow the pattern <code>&lt;city&gt;_&lt;YYYY-MM-DD&gt;.csv</code>, and a city name can contain an underscore (<code>el_jadida_2026-03-01.csv</code>).</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per city and per day with the completed revenue, following these rules:</p>\n<ol><li>city and date come from the file name, not from the content;</li><li>a ride found in several files is kept once, from the file with the earliest date; if the dates are equal, keep the one from the city that comes first alphabetically;</li><li>only completed rides count; compare <code>status</code> ignoring case and surrounding spaces;</li><li>a fare that cannot be parsed counts as <code>0</code>;</li><li>every city and day that has a file appears in the output, with <code>0.0</code> if nothing counts.</li></ol>\n<p>The output must have the columns <code>city</code>, <code>ride_date</code> (date) and <code>revenue_mad</code> (rounded to 2 decimals), sorted by <code>ride_date</code>, then <code>city</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/casablanca_2026-03-01.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">ride_id, Status ,fare_mad\nR1,COMPLETED,45.50\nR2, completed ,\"30,00\"\nR3,cancelled,12.00\nR4,COMPLETED,\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/rabat_2026-03-01.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">Ride_ID,status,FARE_MAD\nR7,completed,61.00\nR1,completed,45.50\n</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>city</th><th>ride_date</th><th>revenue_mad</th></tr><tr><td>casablanca</td><td>2026-03-01</td><td>75.5</td></tr><tr><td>rabat</td><td>2026-03-01</td><td>61.0</td></tr></table></div>\n<p>Ride <code>R1</code> appears in both files of 2026-03-01, so it is kept for <code>casablanca</code> only. <code>R3</code> is cancelled and <code>R4</code> has no fare, so both add nothing.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    rides = spark.read.option(\"header\", True).csv(input_dir)\n    # write your code here\n    return rides\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["lire un dossier","dédoublonnage","Window","nettoyage","try_cast"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"casablanca_2026-03-01.csv":"ride_id, Status ,fare_mad\nR1,COMPLETED,45.50\nR2, completed ,\"30,00\"\nR3,cancelled,12.00\nR4,COMPLETED,\n","rabat_2026-03-01.csv":"Ride_ID,status,FARE_MAD\nR7,completed,61.00\nR1,completed,45.50\n"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"casablanca_2026-03-01.csv":"ride_id, Status ,fare_mad\nR1,COMPLETED,45.50\nR2, completed ,\"30,00\"\nR3,cancelled,12.00\nR4,COMPLETED,\n","rabat_2026-03-01.csv":"Ride_ID,status,FARE_MAD\nR7,completed,61.00\nR1,completed,45.50\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["city","ride_date","revenue_mad"],"rows":[["casablanca","2026-03-01",75.5],["rabat","2026-03-01",61.0]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"el_jadida_2026-03-02.csv":"ride_id,status,fare_mad\nA1,completed,4O.00\nA2,completed,10.00\n","fes_2026-03-01.csv":"ride_id,status,fare_mad\nA2,COMPLETED,99.00\nA3,no_show,5.00\n","fes_2026-03-02.csv":"ride_id,status,fare_mad\nA4,cancelled,8.00\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["city","ride_date","revenue_mad"],"rows":[["fes","2026-03-01",99.0],["el_jadida","2026-03-02",0.0],["fes","2026-03-02",0.0]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}